+## #531 - EDM condition table as user data
+
+**Decided:** `edm.conditions[]` in the `.mch`: `{ id, name, gap, wire_diameter | undersize, role: rough|skim|finish, notes }`.
+- `id` is the control's own selector, required and unique. A numeric id reads as its word.
+- Lengths scale with the file's unit. Gap and undersize may be 0; a wire diameter must be positive.
+- A garbled entry refuses the file, naming its id, and `is_sane` restates the law for project files.
+- `Edm::condition(machine, id, need)` returns the condition with every needed field stated, or the refusal naming the machine, the id and the missing field. It is the door the first EDM op (#532) calls at command creation, so a missing gap or wire diameter is refused before any generator runs.
+- No conditions ship (#290 D4). Tests use an explicitly synthetic table.
+
+**Why:** absent is not zero, and generator data is vendor material. CamCraft needs only the geometry (gap, wire diameter, undersize) to place a path; power and flushing stay the control's, selected by `id`.
+
+**Considered and dropped:**
+- A separate conditions file per machine: the `.mch` is already the machine's statement, and the project file carries it whole.
+- Modelling power, on-time or flushing: that is spark-process physics, out of scope for #290.
+
+**Cost to change later:** low. The section is additive.

From d8fedc81eea32c5f64edcc74b8d8a284742dd311 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:40:12 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] feat(edm): sinker burn to depth with a single electrode

A sinker electrode tool kind (ToolKind::Electrode): diameter = face X,
width = face Y, flute_len = length below the holder, shank_len = pickup
offset; rpm 0 and a sharp face by law, refused by name at AddTool /
ChangeTool / the library reader. EDM-E10X6 joins the starter catalog.

The Sinker Burn op (OpType 41, Section::Sinker, Family::Sinker) runs on
a sinker EDM only - refused by name elsewhere. Depth is read from a
stated datum (work top, cavity floor stand-off, electrode tip at the
approach plane); a burn past the cavity floor datum, past the model's
floor, or deeper than the electrode is long is refused by name. The
machine condition's spark gap (#531, Gap only, after the sinker-kind
check) places the tip one gap above the floor. CL: approach rapid, one
feed plunge, rapid retract; golden tests/golden/sinker_burn_cavity.cl.

Verification (#290 D7): the column engine's box atom (simulate_box)
sweeps the face grown by the gap; the program verdict convicts a burn
deeper than the part's cavity. The field eye refuses an electrode by
name (no box atom there yet). The stamp digests the resolved gap.
MCP drives it through add_tool / add_operation / edit_operation /
generate / undo; a minimal op page keeps the tab law. No post (#542).

Not exercised on a real EDM control.

Fixes #541

